1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,600
Welcome to Pocketful Factory, our submission for the WeAreDevelopers and BAND Dark Factory hackathon.

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:13,662
Our goal was to build a complete bitemporal financial settlement engine without human developers writing business logic.

3
00:00:13,662 --> 00:00:23,387
Inside Band Desktop, we established three distinct agent seats: Architect, Coder, and Auditor, operating under strict generic mandates.

4
00:00:23,387 --> 00:00:27,275
The operator initiates the project directly in the room.

5
00:00:27,275 --> 00:00:32,662
The Architect formalizes financial invariants and dispatches tasks to the Coder.

6
00:00:32,662 --> 00:00:47,062
The Auditor performs rigorous adversarial reviews, catching edge-case bugs and rejecting unverified commits until commit 7b671ec earns final approval, fulfilling all reciprocal messaging requirements of Gate 2.

7
00:00:47,212 --> 00:00:50,312
Here is our official harness verification.

8
00:00:50,262 --> 00:00:54,974
All offline static gates pass cleanly with zero track leaks.

9
00:00:54,974 --> 00:01:04,924
Running the multi-stage evaluation across all four stages, our service achieves a one-hundred percent pass rate across all one hundred and ninety-three conformance tests.

10
00:01:04,924 --> 00:01:11,512
With zero regressions and zero manual workarounds, our factory successfully claims Stage 4.

11
00:01:11,668 --> 00:01:16,918
Now let's examine the generated web client running against our Stage 4 server.

12
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:19,093
We sign in as Ada.

13
00:01:19,093 --> 00:01:23,805
The dashboard displays the real-time available balance and active holds.

14
00:01:23,805 --> 00:01:34,918
When transferring 10 Euros to Bob, the client performs an optimistic update, enforces client idempotency to prevent double-spending, and records the transfer in the activity feed.

15
00:01:34,918 --> 00:01:42,405
Navigating to statements, our bitemporal ledger maintains truthful historical records with exact balance reconciliation.

16
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:46,568
Every stage builds cleanly from an isolated container.

17
00:01:46,568 --> 00:01:48,580
Thank you for watching!

